course: dictionary
lesson: 12991
title: Expiry and time limits
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Expiry means the end of the time when something can still be used. Think of a ticket: once its time has passed, it is no longer valid. «The milk's expiry date is Monday, so drink it before then.» The sentence tells you the milk should not be used after Monday.
explain: The words around expiry are clues. An expiry date is the last day to use food, medicine or a card. «Do not take this medicine after its expiry.» The words after and do not tell you that the time has run out and the medicine is no longer safe.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word: «Do not take this medicine after the end of its usable time.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Expiry means the end of the time when something can be used or is valid.
fact: An «expiry date» is the last day food, medicine or a card should be used.
fact: «On expiry» means when the time runs out.
fact: In the US, people often say «expiration date» instead of «expiry date».
fact: Check the expiry date on food and medicine before you use it.
exercise: «The yoghurt's expiry date was last Tuesday, so we threw it away.» What does expiry date mean here? | The day it was made | The shop it came from | The price of the yoghurt | *The last day it should be used
exercise: Mum says, «Do not take this medicine after its expiry.» What should you do with medicine past its expiry? | Share it with a friend | Take two spoons to be safe | Keep it in the sun | *Do not take it
exercise: Which word in this sentence means the end of the time? «My bus ticket is valid until its expiry on Friday.» | Friday | valid | *expiry | ticket
test: «The passport's expiry is in May, so renew it now.» What does expiry mean here? | The place where you renew it | The colour of the cover | The date when it was printed | *The date when the passport stops being valid
test: Why might a food label use the word expiry instead of just saying end? | It means the food is new | It is a longer word for lunch | It means the food is free | *It is the special word for the last day food can be used
exam: «Before expiry, the card works at any shop; after expiry, it will be refused.» What happens after expiry? | *It stops working | It works only on Sundays | It becomes a new card | It gets cheaper
